Subject: [PATCH 13/23] sheet route: Step 5 report, census of record and its
 evidence

Population of record (2009 cells, Sobol over the trilinear thickness field
and the vertical cut), census at the label module of this branch, the
eight-cell assembly, the rotation action before and after the symmetric
carrier, and the production plan.

Census (commit ff9d147, production preset, surface gates plus the Gmsh
volume): 1946 OK, 59 EMPTY, 3 failures that fail closed, 1 geometry
degenerate.  Two of the three failures are grazing cuts and one is a
generic cell, so the family is an open item, not a closed one.

The report also records what the route does NOT cover, so it is decided
before labels are produced: the cut family reachable by the 48 symmetries
is only the planes parallel to a coordinate axis; one cut plane per cell;
no labels produced across the population yet (the Schur has run on about
25 cells); cut cells never assembled end to end; mesh-dependent zero rows
in the target; and sliver cells, 9.5 percent of the cut bucket, whose
operators are two to three orders of magnitude smaller.

Evidence added under artifacts/.../sheet_true_geometry_label_route_v1:
population census and summary, rotation checks for both carriers, the
same-mesh rotation experiment, the 2x1x1 assembly with the symmetric
carrier, the shared-face trace test for a cut crossing an interface, the
degenerate-cut sweep and four sliver label receipts.
